      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 19057498,
      "version": 995,
      "versionNonce": 862970714,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789961642681,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Whenever we add custom object in HashSet class than we must\noverride equals() and hashcode() method .\n\n2. Whenever we call add() method on HashSet class it does the\nfollowing :\n\n--> It compare the hashcode of object to be added to the hashcode\nof existing object in HashSet .\n\n--> If it doen't find any object with matching hashcode than it add\nthe object to HashSet .\n\n--> But ,if hascode are same of the newly added object to the\nexisting object then it also call the equals object as two different\nobject can have same hashcode .\n\n--> Thus if equals returns true newly object is not added in the \nHashSet .\n\n--> Otherwise it add the object in the hashSet .\n\n--> It is also called hashcode equals contract .\n\n** HashSet store data in hash table",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Whenever we add custom object in HashSet class than we must override equals() and hashcode() method .\n\n2. Whenever we call add() method on HashSet class it does the following :\n\n--> It compare the hashcode of object to be added to the hashcode of existing object in HashSet .\n\n--> If it doen't find any object with matching hashcode than it add the object to HashSet .\n\n--> But ,if hascode are same of the newly added object to the existing object then it also call the equals object as two different object can have same hashcode .\n\n--> Thus if equals returns true newly object is not added in the \nHashSet .\n\n--> Otherwise it add the object in the hashSet .\n\n--> It is also called hashcode equals contract .\n\n** HashSet store data in hash table",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
